# There is No Bubble, There is No Spoon
=> index.gmi Bethany Davis
September 6, 2026

The famous line from the Matrix, "there is no spoon", was never about slight-of-hand or power over reality, it was always about perception. It was a visual symbol to help Neo understand that perception defines what we think we know. We analyze the world based on our preconceived notions of it and what we observe within our own context.

```
People tend to see what they expect to see,
That doesn't make it reality.
```

It's easy to make the comparison between the Dot Com Bubble and what's seen as being what's happening with machine learning (ML) and artificial intelligence (AI). Expecting it to be the same focuses attention not on what's happening in reality but on when the perceived bubble will burst. The assumption is that the parallel between the Dot Com Bubble and now is a true comparison, that all that matters is short term (1-2 year) corporate gains, and that a bubble exists.

That assumption is wrong. Like the spoon, there is no bubble. Unless of course my perception and assumptions are wrong.

```
People tend to see what they expect to see,
That doesn't make it reality.
```

